title The roster claim, read back
prompt Baton lap as Grass -- audit, rota row N mod 5, close what is closable, send.
rota lap 4450, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears. Its own threshold page asks a lap to listen for the claim a page keeps repeating and the silence where a claim used to be. The grain page in the same triad states the strand outright: a guard that cannot red guards nothing, and a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything. Listening for that in this tree's own instruments is what the lap then did.
think The roster construction/standing-equipment.kyri says in its eleventh line that every guard on it can red, citing REDS row 59. That sentence governs 285 files. Its sibling half is walled -- tools/s/standing_equipment_witness.rish gates guards_path_missing at zero and reports never-run guards -- and that witness names its own scope: it proves the mechanics beneath the roster's choice. So one half of row 59 stood behind a gate and the other behind prose.
think Measured by hand first, before writing anything: 285 rostered paths, zero absent, zero tautological asserts, zero files carrying no assert. The claim holds. What was missing was a reading, not a repair.
think A textual marker is a proxy and the header says so. Four spellings this tree already writes -- a prove-red call, a _control.sh invocation, a planted case, an == false assertion -- separate a witness that demonstrates a refusal in its own body from one that leaves the demonstration elsewhere. A looser predicate that also counted the words refusal and must refuse read 23; those words live in assertion messages that co-occur with real markers, so the tight predicate at 53 over-reports rather than under-reports, which is the conservative direction for an audit meter.
obs All 53 counted guards delegate: every one asserts on the result of a real run, so each reds through the child witness, scan, or suite beneath it. Gating that number would refuse every choir the tree owns, which is the gate somebody turns off. Zero-assert is gated; the 53 sit under a ceiling that only falls.
obs What the meter reaches is whether a refusal was demonstrated in the file. Whether that refusal covers the class the guard claims stays a reading a person does, against the grain's own standard: a plant the toothed form bites and the vacuous form would have waved through.
loom redleg guards=285 guards_absent=0 guards_no_assert=0 guards_no_refusal_marker=53 ceiling=53 control_checks=16 control_failures=0
think Reds first, on three the cold pass named. stash_record was mine to close: a Grass lap of 20260909.090354 stood whole in the round-open stash with its session log and five archive shelves, and nothing on disk carried them. Restored by git checkout from the stash tree rather than git show into a file, since a blob carries no mode and the tree object does.
obs The recovered lap also touched construction/ITINERARY.md and the day shelf, which this lap had already edited. Those two were merged by hand rather than taken whole; the seven files it could take were taken byte for byte, and the recital addition proved purely additive against HEAD.
loom stash_record unlanded=1 orphans=5 restored_paths=7 unlanded_after=0 orphans_after=0
think REDS %596 wrote down a falsifier a later lap could run: testimony grew 17 in three days, and the %594 shelf-stamp wall was meant to slow it. This lap ran it. refs_lost 93 -> 98 and lost_testimony 91 -> 94 over two days -- growth from about 5.7 a day to about 1.5. The wall helped substantially and closed nothing, lost_promised_living still reads 0, and the row stays BOOKED on Keaton's word.
loom dated_path refs_lost=98 lost_ceiling=85 lost_testimony=94 lost_living=4 lost_promised_living=0
obs sow_allow_reach refuses on stale projection coverage and names its own repair, a full rescrub of 8,187 files. The scrub standfast on the card has exactly that cost under Keaton's word, so running it inside the standfast about it would be poor judgment. Surfaced rather than taken.
obs standing_equipment reads red from its run card, which is untracked and per pier: one recorded dated_path red from 20260908 on the cadence tier, and one ran fleet_drain row naming a guard renamed to fleet_clockout at 20260908.165143. Both are local ledger state rather than tree faults.
obs Named because it is mine: the cold pass closed tree_moved=yes. I wrote the new scan and control while it ran, and the runner's digest reads untracked files. The hot pass after git add is what measures the tree this commit ships.
loom roster_cold guards_run=212 guards_green=207 guards_red=3 guards_gated=2 guards_seconds=2171 tree_moved=yes
obs Grade what you touch: the first drafts of both headers read 58, an F, on register alone -- 60 and 50 percent negative sentences, because they described the meter by what a guard lacks. Rewritten to lead with what is, both stand at 85. The control reads 100 and the roster page 89.
loom qa artifacts=4 minimum_composite=85 scan=85 witness=85 control=100 roster=89
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_redleg_scan.sh the meter that reads the roster's own claim back
file tools/s/standing_equipment_redleg_witness.rish the rung that gates zero-assert and holds the falling ceiling
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_redleg_control.sh sixteen behaviors on a pen, every refusal planted and lifted
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the row that makes the new reading audible every lap
file construction/ITINERARY.md the Grass live front and this lap's account
file construction/archive/20260909-152755_itinerary-landed-accounts.md the departing Grass front, shelved whole
file session-logs/date/20260909/20260909-090354_five-shelves-find-their-readers.kyri the stranded Grass lap, recovered from its stash
file construction/archive/REDS-fold-recital.md three recovered forwarding addresses, additive against HEAD
file session-logs/date/README-index-20260909.md both rows on the day shelf
recommend keep-going the 53 delegating guards are a ceiling to walk down one lap at a time, starting where a witness reds through a child that itself demonstrates nothing. Keaton's word is what dated_path and the scrub standfast both wait on.
scope The red-leg meter over the standing roster, the recovery of one stranded Grass lap, and a falsifier %596 wrote down
status GREEN -- standing_equipment_redleg green on metal with 16 control checks; standing_equipment_witness green over 286 rows; stash_record verdict=ok, unlanded 1 -> 0 and orphans 5 -> 0; four artifacts grade 85 or better. Open and not mine: dated_path at 98 against 85, BOOKED on Keaton's word under %596; sow_allow_reach under the scrub standfast. Named as mine: the cold pass closed tree_moved=yes because I wrote files while it ran. The staged hot pass and both pushes follow this written verdict.
